hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2701","**
Narrated to us Bundār, narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar, narrated to us Shuʿbah, from Salamah (who is Ibn Kuhayl), who said: I heard Muslim al-Baṭīn, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās (RA), who said:
""During the pre-Islamic period, a woman would perform Tawāf around the House (Kaʿbah) while naked, saying: 'Today, part of him or all of him will be revealed. So whatever part of him is revealed, I will not make it permissible (for myself).'
Then the verse was revealed:
' O children of Adam, take your adornment at every masjid...' (Qur’ān 7:31)."""
"2702","**
Narrated to us ‘Īsā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ghāfiqī:
On the authority of Ibn Wahb, from Yūnus ibn Yazīd and ‘Amr ibn al-Ḥārith, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sa‘īd ibn al-Musayyib, that he used to say:
*""The Day of Sacrifice is the Day of the Greatest Hajj.""*

Ibn Shihāb said, narrated to us from Ḥumayd ibn ‘Abd al-Raḥmān ibn ‘Awf, from Abū Hurayrah (RA), that he said:
*""Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (RA) sent me during the Hajj in which the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) appointed him as commander before the Farewell Hajj, with a group of people. They were to announce to the people on the Day of Sacrifice: ‘No polytheist shall perform Hajj after this day, and no naked person shall perform Tawāf around the House.’""*

Ibn Shihāb said, and Ḥumayd used to say:
*""The Day of Sacrifice is the Day of the Greatest Hajj,""* because of the hadith of Abū Hurayrah (RA)."
